# Consolidate "Concepts" + "Concepts graph"

## Goal
- One Settings tab instead of two.
- Clicking a concept node in the graph opens that concept's **settings** (not the instance browser, which is where it goes today).

## What exists today
- **Concepts** tab (admin-only): text-list of concepts on the left  +  name/description/fields editor on the right. (`Concepts.tsx`)
- **Concepts graph** tab (all members): React-Flow LR diagram, nodes=concepts, edges=relation fields. Node click -> `/concepts/:id` instance browser. (`ConceptsGraph.tsx`)

So we already have a master-detail editor. The merge = swap the text-list "master" for the graph as the selector, keep the detail editor.

---

## Option A — Graph canvas + right drawer  (recommended)
Graph owns the tab. Click a node -> settings slide in on the right; graph stays visible.

```
Settings   [Profile][Organization][Members][ Concepts ]
+----------------------------------------------------------+
| Concepts                                  [+ New concept] |
+-------------------------------------------+--------------+
|                                           | Player    [x]|
|   +--------+   owns    +--------+          |--------------|
|   | Player |---------->| Estate |          | Name         |
|   +--------+           +--------+          | [Player    ] |
|       |                                    | Description  |
|       | rival                              | [..........] |
|       v                                    |              |
|   +--------+                               | Fields    [+]|
|   | House  |                               |  name   text |
|   +--------+                               |  gold   money|
|                                            |  owns -> Est |
|   (pan / zoom canvas)                      |              |
|                                            | [View rows]  |
|                                            | [Save][Del]  |
+-------------------------------------------+--------------+
```
+ Graph is the spatial home; editing in context.
- Drawer overlaps canvas; a bit more new code (drawer state/animation).

## Option B — Persistent split: graph left / editor right
Closest to today's master-detail; lowest-risk reuse of `Concepts.tsx` editor.

```
Settings  >  Concepts
+----------------------------------+----------------------+
| graph canvas          [+ New]    | Player               |
|  +--------+    +--------+         | Name [Player       ] |
|  | Player |--->| Estate |         | Desc [............]  |
|  +--------+    +--------+         | Fields          [+]  |
|       |                           |  name   text         |
|       v                           |  gold   money        |
|  +--------+                       |  owns   -> Estate    |
|  | House  |                       | [View rows]          |
|  +--------+                       | [Save]      [Delete] |
+----------------------------------+----------------------+
```
+ Detail always visible, no overlay; mostly a layout swap.
- Graph gets ~60% width; editor + fields can feel cramped side-by-side.

## Option C — Graph on top / editor below
```
Settings > Concepts
+----------------------------------------------------------+
| graph canvas                            [+ New concept]  |
|   +--------+   +--------+   +--------+                    |
|   | Player |-->| Estate |   | House  |                    |
|   +--------+   +--------+   +--------+                    |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
| Player                                  [Save] [Delete]  |
| Name [Player       ]  Desc [.....................]       |
| Fields                                            [+]    |
|  name text | gold money | owns -> Estate(many) ...       |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
```
+ Editor gets full width (good when fields list is long).
- Graph height is squeezed; more vertical scrolling.

---

## Open questions
1. **Admin gating.** Editor is admin-only today; graph is all-members. Merged tab -> admin-only (non-admins lose the graph), or keep graph readable by all with editor disabled for them?
2. **Reach the instance browser.** Node-click currently jumps to instances; that becomes "open settings". Keep a path via a "View rows" link in the detail pane? (sidebar + dashboard already link to instances, so not the only path.)
3. **Layout** A / B / C.
4. **Tab label** after merge — keep "Concepts", drop "Concepts graph"?

---

## Decisions (locked)
- **Layout A** — graph fills the tab; node-click opens a **right drawer** with that concept's settings. Graph stays visible.
- **Access: read-only for members** — all members see graph + can open a concept's drawer; Save / Delete / Add-field / Edit-field disabled unless admin.
- **Node-click focuses the concept for editing** (opens its drawer).
- Merged tab keeps label **"Concepts"**; the separate "Concepts graph" tab is removed.

## Build plan
1. **`ui.tsx`** — add a right-anchored `Drawer` (esc-to-close + backdrop), mirroring `Modal`.
2. **`ConceptGraphCanvas.tsx`** (new) — extract `buildFlow` / node+edge types / `Flow` out of `ConceptsGraph.tsx`; expose `onSelect(conceptId)` + `selectedId` (highlight active node) instead of `navigate(...)`.
3. **`Concepts.tsx`** (becomes the merged page) — graph canvas + `[+ New concept]` toolbar; `selectedId` opens the `Drawer` holding the existing name/description + fields editor (reused as-is). Consume `admin` from outlet context to gate every mutation control. Optional `[View rows]` link → `/concepts/:id`.
4. **Cache** — concept + field mutations also `invalidateQueries(["conceptGraph"])` so the canvas reflects renames / new relations; after create, select the new node.
5. **`SettingsLayout.tsx`** — drop the `concepts-graph` tab; flip `concepts` tab to `admin: false` (members get read-only).
6. **`App.tsx`** — remove the `concepts-graph` route.
7. Delete `ConceptsGraph.tsx` once its canvas is extracted.

## Unresolved
1. Drawer: overlay canvas (~420px) vs push/resize it? (proposing overlay.)
2. Members: show the drawer with disabled controls, or hide it entirely? (proposing show, disabled.)
3. Keep the `[View rows]` link to the instance browser, or leave instances to the sidebar/dashboard only?
4. `[+ New concept]`: inline create-row (like today) vs small modal? (proposing inline.)
